On Sat, Dec 6, 2014 at 2:28 AM, <ravas@outlook.com> wrote:

>
> Now I'm wondering how da'i and ju'ocui compare.
>

"ju'o cu'i" indicates that the speaker in not quite certain that the
proposition is true. It corresponds to English "perhaps" or "maybe".

   ju'o cu'i do pu tolcpa lo do santa lo sorpeka
   Perhaps you left your umbrella in the bus.

"da'i" indicates that the proposition is not factual. It corresponds to
English "would".

  da'i la .alis. pu banli lo ka mamta
  Alice would have been a great mother.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

